BT /F1 11 Tf 14 TL 72 740 Td
(4. Annual leave) Tj T*
(Full-time employees receive 25 days of paid annual leave per year, plus public) Tj T*
(holidays. Part-time employees receive leave in proportion to their hours.) Tj T*
(Up to 5 unused days can be carried over to the next year; any other unused) Tj T*
(days expire on 31 March of the following year.) Tj T*
(Request leave in the HR portal at least two weeks in advance for periods) Tj T*
(longer than three days.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5. Sick leave) Tj T*
(Tell your manager before 10:00 on the first day you are sick. You need a) Tj T*
(doctor's note from the fourth consecutive sick day. Sick leave is paid in full) Tj T*
(for up to 30 days per year.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(6. Parental leave) Tj T*
(Primary caregivers receive 20 weeks of paid parental leave. Secondary) Tj T*
(caregivers receive 6 weeks. Parental leave can be taken in up to three blocks) Tj T*
(within 18 months of the birth or adoption.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
